  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nA large area of high pressure will slowly drift south across \nthe Northeast into the mid Atlantic region through the weekend. \nSubsidence form the high will provide continued dry conditions, \nmainly sunny/clear skies and light winds. Early morning lows \nwill be chilly in the 20s to lower 30s, but highs should warm to\nnormal levels today (mainly mid/upper 50s) and slightly above \nnormal Sunday (upper 50s to lower 60s). A cold front approaching\nfrom SE Canada looks to move southeastward across the area on \nMon, but due to limited moisture no precip is anticipated with \njust a period of increasing clouds. Ahead of the cold front, \ntemperatures will be be mild Mon with highs in the upper 50s to \nupper 60s. Cooler temperatures will filter in for Tue/Wed behind\nthe cold front with both days expected to be below normal, but \ncontinued dry as high pressure builds in. Milder temperatures \nreturn Thu/Fri, as another cold front may approach late next \nweek, again with limited moisture.",
